                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0e9e0544-dbe0-3599-9199-a19d6c3a7a9d",
                        "entry_id": "3d8502ed-1390-3342-ab41-66f538687d76",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Gentilice, nom de la gens porté par les Romains."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b65b412-6b95-4b20-92e4-e0daaa4698fb",
                                "sense_id": "0e9e0544-dbe0-3599-9199-a19d6c3a7a9d",
                                "text": "L’Histoire mentionne le plus souvent les seuls nomen et cognomen, voire uniquement le cognomen des Romains célèbres."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e5949b2e-8a24-4aa3-9bff-8a0dca63fd7a",
                                "sense_id": "0e9e0544-dbe0-3599-9199-a19d6c3a7a9d",
                                "text": "Les Romains avaient trois noms : le prénom (praenomen) qui désignait l’individu ; le nom (nomen) qui distinguait la gens ou race à laquelle l’individu appartenait ; et le cognomen, qui marquait la branche, la famille ; quelquefois à ces trois noms s’en joignait un quatrième : le surnom (agnomen), tiré d’une action remarquable ou de quelque circonstance extraordinaire : ainsi Publius Cornelius Scipio Africanus."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "268bc4e4-289e-47af-bfdb-c6033315e5fd",
                                "sense_id": "0e9e0544-dbe0-3599-9199-a19d6c3a7a9d",
                                "text": "Ils [les Romains] prennent souvent deux, trois, et jusqu’à quatre noms : nomen, prænomen, cognomen et agnomen.\nLe nom, nomen, était, comme il est encore, le nom d’une maison, commun à tous les membres d’une même souche, et se terminait ordinairement en ius. Il dérivait quelquefois du prénom, prænomen […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "935f170b-0b74-4439-a90d-d9eee62c24c7",
                        "source_entry_id": "3d8502ed-1390-3342-ab41-66f538687d76",
                        "source_sense_id": "0e9e0544-dbe0-3599-9199-a19d6c3a7a9d",
                        "source_sense_description": "nom de la gens porté par les Romains",
                        "target_lang_word": "Nomen",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Nomen",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8e125166-e0ae-3c3f-8c6c-89ab92f4bf11",
                                        "entry_id": "9f4209a9-fbef-3fa3-984e-f1ae1237db0a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Oberbegriff aller deklinierbaren Wortarten"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1a\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e26be0c-c20b-3273-963d-92f877b5e6d5",
                                        "entry_id": "9f4209a9-fbef-3fa3-984e-f1ae1237db0a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Oberbegriff für Substantiv und Adjektiv"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "949bd840-58cb-4e2f-8de3-fa2e7246787e",
                                                "sense_id": "5e26be0c-c20b-3273-963d-92f877b5e6d5",
                                                "text": "„Unter einem Nomen (Adjektiv: nominal) verstehen wir ein Substantiv oder Adjektiv (meist ein Substantiv)…“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0992d083-fcd6-4842-8ece-ef6755b48f8f",
                                                "sense_id": "5e26be0c-c20b-3273-963d-92f877b5e6d5",
                                                "text": "„Vom Nomine, insbesondere dem Substantivo. Ein Nomen (Nennwort) ist entweder ein Substantivum (Hauptwort) oder Adjektivum (Beywort). Ein Nomen substantivum ist die Benennung einer Person oder Sache, wo man im Deutschen der, oder die, oder das, oder ein, eine, ein vorsetzt, als homo der Mensch, terra die Erde, frumentum das Getraide, annus ein Jahr. Ist die Bennung nur Einer Person oder Sache eigen, so heißt sie ein Nomen proprium (ein eigner Name); dergleichen sind alle Vor- und Zunamen der Menschen, die Namen der Länder, Städte, Berge, Flüsse rc.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1b\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e06d9a12-bd3a-3b69-a52d-9f80fbe6c08d",
                                        "entry_id": "9f4209a9-fbef-3fa3-984e-f1ae1237db0a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym zu Substantiv (Hauptwort)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "jünger"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a02d300d-ac03-4a22-b307-798cb6677767",
                                                "sense_id": "e06d9a12-bd3a-3b69-a52d-9f80fbe6c08d",
                                                "text": "Das Wort „Auto“ ist ein Nomen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "334a7425-ed1d-44ff-8bf4-094dbcfd841b",
                                                "sense_id": "e06d9a12-bd3a-3b69-a52d-9f80fbe6c08d",
                                                "text": "„Die kritischen Aussagen verweisen meistens auf die Flexion des Nomens und des Adjektivs und monieren implizit die Mißverhältnisse zwischen Formenvielfalt und Leistungen in den Bereichen Genus, Numerus und Kasus.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "780abea9-9580-4a7f-b26f-3e5a201faf31",
                                                "sense_id": "e06d9a12-bd3a-3b69-a52d-9f80fbe6c08d",
                                                "text": "„Jedes Nomen/Substantiv hat ein Genus, ein grammatisches Geschlecht.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "efa795e7-cd0d-4d90-abe6-55889e2d493d",
                                                "sense_id": "e06d9a12-bd3a-3b69-a52d-9f80fbe6c08d",
                                                "text": "„Dabei nehmen wir eine Beschränkung auf Nomen vor, da diese sich mit Bildvorlagen relativ leicht elizitieren lassen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f88942ea-f691-4485-b230-c833cd35f377",
                                                "sense_id": "e06d9a12-bd3a-3b69-a52d-9f80fbe6c08d",
                                                "text": "„Am besten ist es deshalb, die deutschen Nomen immer mit den Artikeln auswendig zu lernen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a764ae19-dc0f-32c5-b1a0-b5b13cb2673c",
                                        "entry_id": "9f4209a9-fbef-3fa3-984e-f1ae1237db0a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "No glosses available"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "no-gloss"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64a5c86b-5c47-4096-9ddb-2285c0fc27eb",
                                                "sense_id": "a764ae19-dc0f-32c5-b1a0-b5b13cb2673c",
                                                "text": "Die Wörter „Auto“ und „gut\" sind Nomen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7aca7942-1a0f-410e-aaff-e6e4f5892b36",
                                                "sense_id": "a764ae19-dc0f-32c5-b1a0-b5b13cb2673c",
                                                "text": "„Von dem Nomine Substantivo, oder dem Hauptworte.“ (Überschrift)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b948ff2-3f67-44e4-b649-9362b3439bbd",
                                                "sense_id": "a764ae19-dc0f-32c5-b1a0-b5b13cb2673c",
                                                "text": "Das Wort „Auto“ ist ein Nomen."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "67cf6845-7ab1-4a48-8099-fdc2c1199ea7",
                        "source_entry_id": "3d8502ed-1390-3342-ab41-66f538687d76",
                        "source_sense_id": "0e9e0544-dbe0-3599-9199-a19d6c3a7a9d",
                        "source_sense_description": "nom de la gens porté par les Romains",
                        "target_lang_word": "nomen",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "nomen",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "75feeb9f-f709-3518-9efa-e57f67d2751f",
                                        "entry_id": "0c9eb6c3-1269-3fb7-aac0-7cfd3a45a87e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The family name of an Ancient Roman, designating their gens."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac7b4e43-b6e7-41df-b395-3a0a2b3ca194",
                                                "sense_id": "75feeb9f-f709-3518-9efa-e57f67d2751f",
                                                "text": "The Romans evolved a quite different system of nomenclature, which in its classical form consisted of three names, the praenomen (e.g. Marcus), nomen (e.g. Tullius), and cognomen (e.g. Cicero), and two other designations (the name of the father and of the tribe): […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac062a63-da18-4ceb-a66d-ddaf5989595e",
                                                "sense_id": "75feeb9f-f709-3518-9efa-e57f67d2751f",
                                                "text": "Greeks and other provincials who gained Roman citizenship kept their Greek names as cognomens, to which they added Roman nomens and praenomens—usually those of the ones to whom they owed their citizenship."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79dc7bae-330e-33e8-89a9-158ac2b0d17e",
                                        "entry_id": "0c9eb6c3-1269-3fb7-aac0-7cfd3a45a87e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The birth name of a pharaoh, the fifth of the five names of the royal titulary, traditionally encircled by a cartouche and preceded by the title zꜣ-rꜥ."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de32366d-97e3-40f3-ad58-caea5cf02713",
                                                "sense_id": "79dc7bae-330e-33e8-89a9-158ac2b0d17e",
                                                "text": "The adytum is unsculptured, but two monoliths within it bear the name of Physcon and Cleopatra; and in the front chamber of the naos is that of the Ethiopian king “Ashar (Atar)-Amun*, the everliving,” who in some of his nomens is called “the beloved of Isis.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "605409f6-8570-400c-b0c0-8dd137231111",
                                                "sense_id": "79dc7bae-330e-33e8-89a9-158ac2b0d17e",
                                                "text": "The following is a list of the prenomens and nomens of Egyptian kings which are of common occurrence, with transliterations into Roman letters."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "97ceb23b-b9f2-3caf-808c-61737b8b74d9",
                                        "entry_id": "0c9eb6c3-1269-3fb7-aac0-7cfd3a45a87e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A taxonomic name."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd35bf95-19e7-493c-99fb-9a9dbafe5c8c",
                                                "sense_id": "97ceb23b-b9f2-3caf-808c-61737b8b74d9",
                                                "text": "Over the decades and centuries, Linnaeus’s binominal system reached ever greater prominence as a standard to categorize and stabilize organismal biology, and it became necessary to trace taxon names, so that duplication and confusion could be addressed or avoided. As a consequence, different areas of biology developed 'codes' of nomenclature, according to which the availability of such nomina could be governed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
